DESCRIPTION:In dialogue with our upcoming The Threads That Connect Us exhi
 bition\, this workshop uses found imagery\, vintage ephemera\, and contemp
 orary materials to reflect on memory\, place\, and the textures of everyda
 y life. Participants will create layered works that balance personal narra
 tive with broader cultural reference. Emphasis will be placed on editing\,
  composition\, and allowing materials to suggest meaning rather than worki
 ng toward a fixed outcome. All experience levels are welcome. Instructors 
 : Robin Borelli\, Laura Engdahl\, and Jen Siddens May 16\, 2026 12:00pm 
 – 4:00pm $150 Members\, $170 Non-Members Materials : Two 12” x 12” w
 ood panels and heavy art paper&nbsp\;are provided and included in the pric
 e.&nbsp\; A supply list of other art supplies for participants to bring wi
 ll be provided upon registration.&nbsp\;Participants are also encouraged t
 o bring copies of personal photographs\, letters\, maps\, or printed matte
 r that feel connected to their own sense of personal history\, though some
  shared collage materials will also be provided. #block-7a14000312225e29e9
