DESCRIPTION:In our North Gallery\, photographer Arthur Drooker presents se
 lections from Thirty-Six Views of the Golden Gate Bridge \, a photographic
  series inspired by the celebrated 19th-century Japanese artist Katsushika
  Hokusai and his iconic series Thirty-Six Views of Mount Fuji . Nearly two
  centuries later\, Drooker undertakes a similar artistic exploration\, tur
 ning his lens toward Golden Gate Bridge—the defining landmark of San Fra
 ncisco. View the related Expressions in Metal Exhibit in the main gallery 
 here. ‍ #block-742bb3ed58541b8cc175 { } #block-742bb3ed58541b8cc175 .sqs
